{
 "_readme": "Clash of Clans art used under Supercell's Fan Content Policy. Sourced from the community wiki (clashofclans.fandom.com) and served as WebP. Files are named by content hash and shared wherever the art is identical.",
 "_policy": "https://supercell.com/en/fan-content-policy/",
 "_source": "https://clashofclans.fandom.com",
 "_structures": "public/sprites/*.webp, indexed by src/lib/sprites/buildings.json. Indexed per LEVEL, because the village shows a structure at the level it is. Levels are the ceiling each Town Hall reaches, from src/lib/game/buildings.ts; the wiki holds stray uploads (Archer_Tower109, Air_Defense2012 - a typo and a year), so the game data caps which files are considered. A level with no entry uses the highest entry below it.",
 "_units": "public/sprites/units/*.webp, indexed by src/lib/sprites/units.json. ONE portrait per unit, not one per level, because that is what the game's own Laboratory and Army screens show. Keyed 'village:id' - the home and Builder Base villages share unit ids (Baby Dragon) but not necessarily their art.",
 "_resources": "public/sprites/resources/*.webp, indexed by src/lib/sprites/resources.json. ONE badge per resource per village, no levels. Keyed 'village:kind' because Builder Gold and Builder Elixir are SEPARATE currencies from the home village's - they cannot be moved between villages and the game draws them differently (a gold plate, a violet drop). The Builder Base has no dark elixir, so that key has no builder entry. A badge marks a COST; an amount already banked is marked with the storage that holds it, which is a structure and indexed per level.",
 "_builder": "public/sprites/builder/*.webp, indexed by src/lib/sprites/builder-buildings.json. Builder Base structure art, indexed per LEVEL like the Home Village's. Kept in a separate index rather than under prefixed ids because the two villages share structure names - both have a Cannon, a Gold Storage and an Army Camp - and look nothing alike; separate indexes mean a missing Builder Base sprite can never resolve to the Home Village one. The wiki files these with a 'B' suffix (Cannon7B.png), sometimes with a _Ground/_Air state, and files the B.O.B Control under its old name, O.T.T.O Hut.",
